@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Fine Jewelry Care & Cleaning Guide — SAT Jewel";
}

<div class="care-guide-page">
    <!-- Header Section -->
    <div class="care-header">
        <h1 class="care-main-title">Moissanite &amp; Lab Diamond Jewelry Care Guide</h1>
        <p class="care-subtitle">"Take care of your jewelry and it will shine for years. Follow these simple steps to keep your lab diamonds and fine jewelry looking brand new."</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 6 Core Care Rules Grid (Matching User Image 4) -->
    <div class="care-rules-container">
        <div class="care-rules-grid">
            <!-- Rule 1 -->
            <div class="care-rule-card">
                <div class="care-rule-icon">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-spray-can-sparkles"></i>
                </div>
                <p class="care-rule-text">Avoid spraying perfume directly on your jewelry. Always wear your jewelry after you've sprayed your perfume, best avoiding your neck or wrists.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Rule 2 -->
            <div class="care-rule-card">
                <div class="care-rule-icon">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-shower"></i>
                </div>
                <p class="care-rule-text">We recommend removing your jewelry before stepping into the shower as well as rings before hand-washing to keep it shiny for longer.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Rule 3 -->
            <div class="care-rule-card">
                <div class="care-rule-icon">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-pump-soap"></i>
                </div>
                <p class="care-rule-text">Lotions &amp; creams may contain acidic ingredients that react with your pieces. Avoid moisturizing areas of skin that get in contact with your pieces.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Rule 4 -->
            <div class="care-rule-card">
                <div class="care-rule-icon">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-box-archive"></i>
                </div>
                <p class="care-rule-text">Store your jewelry pieces in a cool, dry place in a box or pouch that comes with your pieces to prevent accidental scratches.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Rule 5 -->
            <div class="care-rule-card">
                <div class="care-rule-icon">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-person-swimming"></i>
                </div>
                <p class="care-rule-text">Avoid swimming with your pieces as chlorine &amp; sea water will react with fine metals and cause settings to tarnish.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Rule 6 -->
            <div class="care-rule-card">
                <div class="care-rule-icon">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-bed"></i>
                </div>
                <p class="care-rule-text">Remove your pieces before going to bed to avoid any accidental snagging that may cause damage to fine prongs or chains.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Detailed Cleaning Guide & Tools Sidebar (Matching User Image 5) -->
    <div class="care-detail-container">
        <div class="care-detail-layout">
            <!-- Left Column: Detailed Cleaning Methods -->
            <div class="care-methods-col">
                <h2 class="care-section-heading">How To Care For &amp; Clean Your Fine Jewelry</h2>
                <p class="care-para">Protect your pieces from sharp blows, scratches, chemicals, and abrasives. The jewelry we make is delicate and not meant to be worn during activities such as sports, swimming, gardening, or heavy cleaning. When not in use, it is best to store your jewelry pieces in airtight zip bags or soft anti-tarnish pouches.</p>

                <h3 class="care-sub-heading">How To Clean Oxidized Silver</h3>
                <p class="care-para">Oxidation is the intentional blackening of silver by dipping it in a chemical solution. It is a semi-permanent treatment that lightens over time with wear. A coating of food-grade wax has been applied to prolong the color, but precautions should still be taken.</p>
                <p class="care-para">To protect the surface color, avoid contact with lotions, perfumes, etc. Remove rings when washing hands and do not wear your jewelry in the shower or to sleep.</p>

                <h3 class="care-sub-heading">How To Clean Sterling Silver &amp; Gold</h3>
                <p class="care-para">Sterling silver is an alloy containing 92.5% by weight of silver and 7.5% by weight of other metals. While contact with air will cause the surface of silver to darken (tarnish), it is easily cleaned up with a soft polishing cloth or using a gentle home wash method.</p>
                <p class="care-para">Fill a glass with warm water, add a few drops of mild dish soap, and soak your diamond ring for 10 to 15 minutes. Gently brush around the diamond setting using a soft-bristled toothbrush, then rinse with clean water and pat dry with a microfiber cloth.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Right Column: Tools And Materials You Need Sidebar -->
            <div class="care-sidebar-col">
                <div class="care-tools-card">
                    <h3 class="care-tools-title">Tools And Materials You Need</h3>

                    <div class="care-tool-item">
                        <img src="/assets/ivevar/WhatsApp_Image_2025-05-20_at_17.52.31_7e9aa222.jpg" alt="Tarnished Silver Jewelry" />
                        <span>Tarnished Silver Jewelry</span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="care-tool-item">
                        <img src="/assets/ivevar/WhatsApp_Image_2025-05-20_at_17.52.38_a7c38636.jpg" alt="Tin-Foil Paper" />
                        <span>Tin-Foil Paper</span>
                    </div>

                    <div class="care-tool-item">
                        <img src="/assets/ivevar/WhatsApp_Image_2025-05-21_at_09.56.16_1378a17a.jpg" alt="Hot Water" />
                        <span>Warm Clean Water</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<style>
    .care-guide-page {
        background-color: #faf8f5;
        color: #1a1a1a;
        font-family: 'Plus Jakarta Sans', sans-serif;
        padding-bottom: 80px;
    }

    .care-header {
        text-align: center;
        padding: 60px 20px 30px;
        background: #ffffff;
    }

    .care-main-title {
        font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
        font-size: 2.8rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #111827;
        margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    .care-subtitle {
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        color: #6b7280;
        max-width: 780px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        line-height: 1.6;
        font-style: italic;
    }

    .care-rules-container {
        background: #f4efe6;
        padding: 60px 24px;
    }

    .care-rules-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
        gap: 24px;
        max-width: 1200px;
        margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .care-rule-card {
        background: #ffffff;
        border-radius: 12px;
        padding: 32px 24px;
        text-align: center;
        border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
        box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.03);
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        align-items: center;
    }

    .care-rule-icon {
        width: 60px;
        height: 60px;
        border-radius: 50%;
        background: #fdf8f0;
        color: #b45309;
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        justify-content: center;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
        border: 1px solid #fce8cc;
    }

    .care-rule-text {
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        color: #4b5563;
        line-height: 1.65;
        margin: 0;
    }

    /* Detailed Section Layout */
    .care-detail-container {
        max-width: 1200px;
        margin: 60px auto 0;
        padding: 0 24px;
    }

    .care-detail-layout {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr;
        gap: 40px;
    }

    .care-section-heading {
        font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
        font-size: 2.2rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #111827;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    .care-sub-heading {
        font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #111827;
        margin: 28px 0 12px;
    }

    .care-para {
        font-size: 1rem;
        color: #4b5563;
        line-height: 1.8;
        margin-bottom: 16px;
    }

    /* Sidebar Card */
    .care-tools-card {
        background: #ffffff;
        border-radius: 16px;
        padding: 28px 24px;
        border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
        box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
    }

    .care-tools-title {
        font-family: 'Playfair Display', Georgia, serif;
        font-size: 1.4rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #111827;
        margin-bottom: 24px;
    }

    .care-tool-item {
        display: flex;
        align-items: center;
        gap: 16px;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
        padding-bottom: 20px;
        border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f5f9;
    }

    .care-tool-item:last-child {
        margin-bottom: 0;
        padding-bottom: 0;
        border-bottom: none;
    }

    .care-tool-item img {
        width: 80px;
        height: 80px;
        border-radius: 10px;
        object-fit: cover;
        border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    }

    .care-tool-item span {
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        color: #334155;
    }

    @@media (max-width: 992px) {
        .care-rules-grid {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }
        .care-detail-layout {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }
    }
</style>
